# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the worker corpus (scripts/tsan-workers.mjs).
# One `race:<name>` line per known race, under a comment that says why it is
# tolerated and what removes the line.

# Every context that first uses a message port, the main thread and each
# worker, installs the port operations by storing the address of one static
# table in the global scr_message_port_ops (scr_port_ops_install in
# scr_worker_events.c), and other threads read that global. Every store
# writes the same pointer, so a reader sees NULL before the first install
# or that address; it is still an unsynchronized write to shared memory.
# Storing it once, or atomically, removes this line.
race:scr_message_port_ops
